#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063923 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9911dc0d-905d-54e1-aadb-f4fbce6f89d2" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Tangent Function"}] :question/id #uuid "75114520-8891-503c-81b7-be4c86f5d054" :question/math-academy-id "e-202" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $y = \\arctan (-7x).$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of arctangent is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arctan x) = \\dfrac{1}{1+x^2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-7x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+(-7x)^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-7x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+49{x}^{2}}\\cdot (-7) \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{1+49{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063924 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "93a44f44-0998-5857-9b12-de8998e370fd" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Cosine Function"}] :question/id #uuid "c0a82f3e-9e04-50ce-b3b2-54fafd4c1db8" :question/math-academy-id "e-203" :question/problem "Calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x},$ if $y = \\arccos (5-8x).$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of arccosine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arccos x) = -\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(5-8x)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(5-8x)^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5-8x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(25-80x+64{x}^{2})}}\\cdot (-8) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{80x-24-64{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{4(20x-6-16{x}^{2})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{2\\sqrt{20x-6-16{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{20x-6-16{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063925 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5582e8b-3870-5a32-b15e-62b8f8306ce6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Trigonometric Functions Using the Product or Quotient Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "0f8652d9-5d83-5d2c-93ae-2f3a4fc4e3e7" :question/math-academy-id "e-204" :question/problem "If $y= x \\arccos x,$ calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the product rule and using the formula for the derivative of $\\arccos x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x) & =x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x)+\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}})+\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}+\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063926 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "552973a7-4ab5-5918-83f4-15ee0e3ee052" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sine Function"}] :question/id #uuid "cbeacfa8-783e-5761-a74a-50b78a19ce20" :question/math-academy-id "e-206" :question/problem "Calculate $f'(x)$ for $f(x) = 5\\arcsin(3x^2).$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of arcsine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arcsin x) = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(3{x}^{2})) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(3{x}^{2})^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{1-9{x}^{4}}}\\cdot (6x) \\\\  & =\\frac{30x}{\\sqrt{1-9{x}^{4}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279768 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "552973a7-4ab5-5918-83f4-15ee0e3ee052" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4acabf1-5c6f-5007-b17b-e0b635de11c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{arcsin}^{4}⁡(4x)}{\\sqrt{1-16{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279770} {:answer/id #uuid "56905950-f720-59be-b08c-48032c9555f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{arcsin}^{4}⁡(2x)}{\\sqrt{1-16{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279771} {:answer/id #uuid "c23d1040-1d8e-5108-b571-ca5eeec240b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20{arcsin}^{4}⁡(4x)}{\\sqrt{1-16{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279772} {:answer/id #uuid "56966280-435a-5f10-9aa9-f094ac59a4c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{arcsin}^{4}⁡(4x)}{\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279773} {:answer/id #uuid "d4a4a4c4-ca44-5d53-b155-95a1cd7de3ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20{arcsin}^{2}⁡(4x)}{\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279774}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c23d1040-1d8e-5108-b571-ca5eeec240b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20{arcsin}^{4}⁡(4x)}{\\sqrt{1-16{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279772} :answer-field/id #uuid "06c317c7-d416-5f37-860b-3dd149b5e6f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279769}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4f7a31dd-33d0-5aed-bd19-1d96e4e6f5ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-110049" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)={arcsin}^{5}⁡(4x).$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of arcsine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{arcsin}^{5}⁡(4x)] \\\\  & =5{arcsin}^{4}⁡(4x)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(4x)] \\\\  & =5{arcsin}^{4}⁡(4x)\\cdot [\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(4x)^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4x)] \\\\  & =5{arcsin}^{4}⁡(4x)\\cdot [\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(4x)^{2}}}\\cdot 4] \\\\  & =5{arcsin}^{4}⁡(4x)\\cdot \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-16{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{20{arcsin}^{4}⁡(4x)}{\\sqrt{1-16{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279775 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "93a44f44-0998-5857-9b12-de8998e370fd" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Cosine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5027aa7b-3abb-5405-bf0a-6b7a0bdecb77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279777} {:answer/id #uuid "9c6ffaa9-b135-518c-8a15-6bbb5404501a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5+\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279778} {:answer/id #uuid "3e617787-30ea-5b51-87b5-3297e7e66b2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x+\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279779} {:answer/id #uuid "46662baf-dbaf-5fa1-a848-ef4c609dd1ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279780} {:answer/id #uuid "5611dd09-3a40-5a7a-918d-617fafd54a02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5-\\frac{4x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279781}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5027aa7b-3abb-5405-bf0a-6b7a0bdecb77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279777} :answer-field/id #uuid "eff66a7a-8cd1-58b6-9920-4fbde340e975" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279776}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6020088e-6350-518e-8a34-5b023a434737" :question/math-academy-id "q-110625" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$  for $f(x)=5x+4\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of arccosine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5x+4\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x) \\\\  & =5+4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x) \\\\  & =5+4(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}) \\\\  & =5-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279782 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "93a44f44-0998-5857-9b12-de8998e370fd" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Cosine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c9af1f7-ae07-5974-a8e8-9114a0e809e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8+\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279784} {:answer/id #uuid "0bf7363d-95d9-5e61-a7e2-d4a77525e5d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8-\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279785} {:answer/id #uuid "fc7cd730-d1c6-53e6-b799-4896b932ffb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15-\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279786} {:answer/id #uuid "d8524822-7a32-54b6-860e-692eb2deb060" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x-\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279787} {:answer/id #uuid "fb99ae55-5d74-57e2-a890-2932f0398e7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8+\\frac{15x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279788}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bf7363d-95d9-5e61-a7e2-d4a77525e5d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8-\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279785} :answer-field/id #uuid "91e3b921-f045-5815-aed7-0a25dd310111" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279783}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6d6be61e-f6db-56ce-b1fc-d0e38bd5fb06" :question/math-academy-id "q-110626" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$  for $f(x)=15\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x+8x.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of arccosine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(15\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x+8x) \\\\  & =15\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x)+8 \\\\  & =15(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}})+8 \\\\  & =8-\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279789 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5582e8b-3870-5a32-b15e-62b8f8306ce6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Trigonometric Functions Using the Product or Quotient Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fcb17cb9-1dc9-5547-8206-67fcaf010514" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}+{x}^{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3})}{({x}^{6}+1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279791} {:answer/id #uuid "31a6d127-4c86-520a-91e0-b79e8c631639" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}-6{x}^{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3})}{({x}^{6}+1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279792} {:answer/id #uuid "d02537ab-4e5e-5934-9da5-d915f258cb2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}-6{x}^{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3})}{({x}^{6}+1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279793} {:answer/id #uuid "68993855-9e0f-5374-8c5c-1dfe7b5bbd42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}-6{x}^{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3})}{({x}^{6}+1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279794} {:answer/id #uuid "2edb6c26-a7ac-515a-9898-9f2c977aeff3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6{x}^{2}+3{x}^{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3})}{({x}^{6}+1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279795}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31a6d127-4c86-520a-91e0-b79e8c631639" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}-6{x}^{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3})}{({x}^{6}+1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279792} :answer-field/id #uuid "64421499-c31b-5404-bb67-f06accba6ef8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279790}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fcc0e0ea-aee2-503a-88a5-a3c1170aa40f" :question/math-academy-id "q-110762" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3})}{{x}^{6}+1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the quotient rule, using the formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ and applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3})}{{x}^{6}+1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{6}+1)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3}))-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{6}+1)}{({x}^{6}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{6}+1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{6}+1}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot 6{x}^{5}}{({x}^{6}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{({x}^{6}+1)(3{x}^{2})}{{x}^{6}+1}-6{x}^{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3})}{({x}^{6}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}-6{x}^{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3})}{({x}^{6}+1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279796 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5582e8b-3870-5a32-b15e-62b8f8306ce6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Trigonometric Functions Using the Product or Quotient Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "911f2d06-ea85-5a5b-92c5-b652ebd6c7de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5x)}{{x}^{2}(10{x}^{2}+1)}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot {arctan}^{2}⁡(5x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279798} {:answer/id #uuid "dc8813d3-c93e-5f62-ae32-de754bf70c62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)}{{x}^{2}(5{x}^{2}+1)}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot {arctan}^{2}⁡(5x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279799} {:answer/id #uuid "7afb0a50-4eca-51d4-9375-ccc7eaeea582" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5x)}{{x}^{2}(25{x}^{2}+1)}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot {arctan}^{2}⁡(5x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279800} {:answer/id #uuid "c271d04b-3818-5365-ae25-0c42db808ed1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5x)}{{x}^{2}(25{x}^{2}+1)}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot {arctan}^{2}⁡(5x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279801} {:answer/id #uuid "01b4c0e8-d8e2-59b4-90bb-e953f119c048" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5x)}{10{x}^{2}(25{x}^{2}+1)}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot {arctan}^{2}⁡(5x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7afb0a50-4eca-51d4-9375-ccc7eaeea582" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5x)}{{x}^{2}(25{x}^{2}+1)}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot {arctan}^{2}⁡(5x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279800} :answer-field/id #uuid "81fa075e-4586-58a1-b3c2-294cf5bdd68a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279797}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3ddbced9-36a4-5d45-b580-8e2051270017" :question/math-academy-id "q-110769" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ if  $f(x)=\\frac{{arctan}^{2}⁡(5x)}{{x}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the quotient rule, using the formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ and applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{{arctan}^{2}⁡(5x)}{{x}^{2}}] \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5x)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5x))-(2x){arctan}^{2}⁡(5x)}{{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5x)\\cdot \\frac{5}{1+(5x)^{2}}-(2x){arctan}^{2}⁡(5x)}{{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5x)}{{x}^{2}(25{x}^{2}+1)}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot {arctan}^{2}⁡(5x).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279803 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5582e8b-3870-5a32-b15e-62b8f8306ce6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Trigonometric Functions Using the Product or Quotient Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06e425c6-6726-5348-9925-742c37d6dd37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279805} {:answer/id #uuid "3a7ac635-cf39-5709-8c14-bfc7038f08ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{e}^{x}}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}+\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279806} {:answer/id #uuid "7646376a-925b-58ba-8c32-4589ec27fdb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279807} {:answer/id #uuid "19707ed5-933e-50e6-8bac-36ffb6d74de0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279808} {:answer/id #uuid "36c26d81-2213-5343-84b7-9cac1ab8df67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}+\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06e425c6-6726-5348-9925-742c37d6dd37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279805} :answer-field/id #uuid "43dfdbfa-b49a-5dc5-ad51-8d99686be7e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279804}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ab199b38-800b-5e42-b55a-d55b29af3540" :question/math-academy-id "q-110777" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the quotient rule and using the formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x,$  we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}) & =\\frac{{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x)-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})}{{({e}^{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x\\cdot {e}^{x}}{{e}^{2x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x)}{{e}^{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279810 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5582e8b-3870-5a32-b15e-62b8f8306ce6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Trigonometric Functions Using the Product or Quotient Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b942c9e5-19b1-5712-b8ce-439a13efc44d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{6}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{2})}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279812} {:answer/id #uuid "750c290e-27e6-5ac3-ad54-93be5f80dff6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{6}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(1)}{x{ln}^{2}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279813} {:answer/id #uuid "11e70d26-0d15-527b-b51a-e07b65305cfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{6}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3})}{x{ln}^{2}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279814} {:answer/id #uuid "e7068ff0-aafa-5e39-96e1-a86a7f6b1c1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{6}}}+\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(3{x}^{2})}{x{ln}^{2}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279815} {:answer/id #uuid "2330fc7b-bbae-5929-a302-b42ceb72d630" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{6}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3})}{x{ln}^{2}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279816}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2330fc7b-bbae-5929-a302-b42ceb72d630" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{6}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3})}{x{ln}^{2}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279816} :answer-field/id #uuid "98f8d937-6a12-5052-af88-faf616fac79e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279811}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "36f2cd74-3dbe-552e-ad6d-a2938b875938" :question/math-academy-id "q-19071" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3})}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the quotient rule, using the formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x$ and applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3})}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3}))-\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}{{ln}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-({x}^{3})^{2}}})\\cdot (3{x}^{2})-\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{6}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3})}{x})}{{ln}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{6}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3})}{x{ln}^{2}⁡x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279817 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9911dc0d-905d-54e1-aadb-f4fbce6f89d2" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7dbcb75f-1a64-5fce-a8c0-7edd8c28ca65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6{e}^{x}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3{e}^{x})}{1+9{e}^{2x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279819} {:answer/id #uuid "e8139565-b2de-52be-92c7-152bfad978d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{e}^{x}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3{e}^{x})}{1+{e}^{2x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279820} {:answer/id #uuid "cb58dd0a-98fa-59b5-b098-4cba9ee94768" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6{e}^{x}}{1+9{e}^{2x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279821} {:answer/id #uuid "5a9cc951-1340-57a6-91fd-a2e8fd7b131f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{x}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3{e}^{x})}{1+3{e}^{2x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279822} {:answer/id #uuid "c74b2ced-f728-52bd-8bd7-fd5fa4418d97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3{e}^{x})}{1+9{e}^{2x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7dbcb75f-1a64-5fce-a8c0-7edd8c28ca65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6{e}^{x}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3{e}^{x})}{1+9{e}^{2x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279819} :answer-field/id #uuid "63da8d0c-b989-5dc3-a662-0e116b58a991" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279818}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "824f3163-7ee2-50bf-ba23-40c7883d87a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-19080" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)={arctan}^{2}⁡(3{e}^{x}).$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of arctangent is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({arctan}^{2}⁡(3{e}^{x})) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3{e}^{x})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3{e}^{x})) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3{e}^{x})\\cdot \\frac{1}{1+{(3{e}^{x})}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3{e}^{x})\\cdot \\frac{1}{1+9{e}^{2x}}\\cdot 3{e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{6{e}^{x}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3{e}^{x})}{1+9{e}^{2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279824 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9911dc0d-905d-54e1-aadb-f4fbce6f89d2" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9cd299b-8b7a-52eb-93f6-7a6d1f9ef036" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{1+(5x-4)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279826} {:answer/id #uuid "b327d83d-0bd6-510e-aced-235697c56348" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+(5x-4)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9cd299b-8b7a-52eb-93f6-7a6d1f9ef036" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{1+(5x-4)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279826} :answer-field/id #uuid "184cb8e7-8d9c-5fb7-b85e-925185d38059" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279825}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7394d353-33a6-52d4-886a-276297e613d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-314735" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5x-4)+2.$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of arctangent is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5x-4)+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+{(5x-4)}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5x-4)+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+{(5x-4)}^{2}}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{1+{(5x-4)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279828 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5582e8b-3870-5a32-b15e-62b8f8306ce6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Trigonometric Functions Using the Product or Quotient Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c99eab68-10a1-54fd-9fa7-abc123d64e8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{(x^2+5)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c99eab68-10a1-54fd-9fa7-abc123d64e8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{(x^2+5)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279830} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bfaffd5-5812-5f57-9643-0251e30476b2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279829}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "24f422e2-3f21-5e44-aa45-bacd5f7d9617" :question/math-academy-id "q-314738" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2{x}^{3})}{{x}^{2}+5}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{6{x}^{2}}{({x}^{2}+5)(1+4{x}^{6})}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2{x}^{3})$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the quotient rule, using the formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ and applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2{x}^{3})}{{x}^{2}+5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(({x}^{2}+5)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2{x}^{3}))-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2{x}^{3})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+5))}{({x}^{2}+5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(({x}^{2}+5)\\cdot \\frac{1}{1+(2{x}^{3})^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3})-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2{x}^{3})\\cdot 2x)}{({x}^{2}+5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{({x}^{2}+5)(6{x}^{2})}{1+4{x}^{6}}-2x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2{x}^{3}))}{({x}^{2}+5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6{x}^{2}}{({x}^{2}+5)(1+4{x}^{6})}-\\frac{2x}{({x}^{2}+5)^{2}}\\,\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2{x}^{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279831 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "93a44f44-0998-5857-9b12-de8998e370fd" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Cosine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57ce04bb-17bd-556d-b90e-fc774b2b5bce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57ce04bb-17bd-556d-b90e-fc774b2b5bce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279833} :answer-field/id #uuid "962a6808-f67d-54e2-adfe-b0552e4eda8c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279832}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2ac610b2-e98c-5a40-898f-0cdce0bf720c" :question/math-academy-id "q-343050" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\,$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of arccosine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279834 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9911dc0d-905d-54e1-aadb-f4fbce6f89d2" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b461060-4ffc-5fbf-a22e-090954e6a8b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15x^2}{1+25x^6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b461060-4ffc-5fbf-a22e-090954e6a8b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15x^2}{1+25x^6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279836} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9ed7643-ed4d-5e46-99a7-3df37c82b25b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279835}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8dc90ced-2cea-5462-882d-c73f55d8195c" :question/math-academy-id "q-343223" :question/problem "Find ${y}^{′}$ for $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5{x}^{3}).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of arctangent is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5{x}^{3})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+{(5{x}^{3})}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+25{x}^{6}}\\cdot 15{x}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{15{x}^{2}}{1+25{x}^{6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279837 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9911dc0d-905d-54e1-aadb-f4fbce6f89d2" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "417e8c6d-2736-5321-ba7f-aae9f99f5e4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6x^2+1}{1+(2x^3+x)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "417e8c6d-2736-5321-ba7f-aae9f99f5e4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6x^2+1}{1+(2x^3+x)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279839} :answer-field/id #uuid "c76e533b-8311-5bb6-b75d-67ef402afce1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "146698a5-a545-5ee8-a19e-758c40e24662" :question/math-academy-id "q-343687" :question/problem "Find ${y}^{′}$ for $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2{x}^{3}+x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of arctangent is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2{x}^{3}+x)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+{(2{x}^{3}+x)}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}+x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+(2{x}^{3}+x)^{2}}\\cdot (6{x}^{2}+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{6{x}^{2}+1}{1+(2{x}^{3}+x)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279840 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9911dc0d-905d-54e1-aadb-f4fbce6f89d2" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8710538-75df-5870-bb03-bd7b948c57d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279842} {:answer/id #uuid "6821cf03-60b5-545b-ab70-bddb576ba2c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279843}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6821cf03-60b5-545b-ab70-bddb576ba2c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279843} :answer-field/id #uuid "570cec3e-9322-5c68-926d-3833dc9587a5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279841}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7f3323c8-7620-5f06-922a-9c432a075649" :question/math-academy-id "q-343769" :question/problem "Find the exact value of the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve $f(x)=3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{2}-2x)$ at $x=2.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of arctangent is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{2}-2x)] \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{1+({x}^{2}-2x)^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}-2x) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1+{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}}\\cdot (2x-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{6x-6}{{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve $y=f(x)$ at $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={f}^{′}(2) \\\\  & =\\frac{6(2)-6}{(2)^{4}-4(2)^{3}+4(2)^{2}+1} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279844 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "93a44f44-0998-5857-9b12-de8998e370fd" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Cosine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e7f2dbd-d922-5cec-8739-14f594714e90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279846} {:answer/id #uuid "bb18c0b6-b932-5218-a2bc-656320005aa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279847} {:answer/id #uuid "5087f760-e64b-5afb-a504-b14e0bd39127" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279848} {:answer/id #uuid "26f8fa56-10a9-57c2-85c3-8461425bf4c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279849} {:answer/id #uuid "474f4ee1-9c25-58c9-8138-477f5d4b33db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279850}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5087f760-e64b-5afb-a504-b14e0bd39127" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279848} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cb590bd-662e-5bee-bdf0-bf49090ec544" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279845}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dc2a9fc5-8a68-56e3-ba2c-684147dac15a" :question/math-academy-id "q-73488" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$  for $f(x)=5-2\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of arccosine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5-2\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x) \\\\  & =0-2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x) \\\\  & =-2(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279851 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "93a44f44-0998-5857-9b12-de8998e370fd" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Cosine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bce9502-0419-58cf-b883-e33d03730128" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279853} {:answer/id #uuid "f41f8327-21d7-5318-ba53-49be5e032381" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279854} {:answer/id #uuid "e74b74aa-9409-5c07-a9d1-e64144e6d9d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279855} {:answer/id #uuid "0c4d2832-0e56-5858-869b-10f81a4afbf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279856} {:answer/id #uuid "021b6bce-fa11-5f66-acfc-1a6e91101c6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "021b6bce-fa11-5f66-acfc-1a6e91101c6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279857} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3ca59e4-b722-5d73-a348-d559619d9b30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279852}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cbbb8fd8-c714-5582-ac83-4c47b2b5664b" :question/math-academy-id "q-73500" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$  for $f(x)=2x-5\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of arccosine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x-5\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x) \\\\  & =2-5\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x) \\\\  & =2-5(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}) \\\\  & =2+\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279858 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "552973a7-4ab5-5918-83f4-15ee0e3ee052" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff36e148-7e72-5dc4-9410-625a3ab7d71b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279860} {:answer/id #uuid "44cd6e84-2f27-5c50-8df2-bff03d314ae3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279861} {:answer/id #uuid "b9a57ee4-36b1-511f-b3af-4dbda883a583" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279862} {:answer/id #uuid "f1adac43-b31c-5167-9ac5-6435a5aadb2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279863} {:answer/id #uuid "04858987-53fa-587d-833f-b3a470d1c783" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279864}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff36e148-7e72-5dc4-9410-625a3ab7d71b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279860} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f94548a-0b16-58c6-a68d-cb0fc920d870" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279859}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2c302c87-02f5-5482-aedd-0d4c24ffef2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-73507" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=5+9\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of arcsine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5+9\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x) \\\\  & =0+9\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x) \\\\  & =0+9\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279865 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "552973a7-4ab5-5918-83f4-15ee0e3ee052" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aefad1cc-fc7a-5923-adbd-0069e0622775" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}}{8\\sqrt{1+{e}^{2x}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279867} {:answer/id #uuid "9c8adaba-36be-5f3d-abb5-32bf08002db5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8{e}^{2x}}{\\sqrt{1-